":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n- Reproducible in 4.4\n\n### System information\n\nWindows 10, Nvidia, not super relevant to this issue\n\n### Issue description\n\nWhen composing Visual Shaders, and overriding the \"Light\" function, the \"Input\" node is missing Alpha from it's list, which is unlike the Diffuse and Specular in the lighting function.\n\nThis means you cannot properly accumulate alpha values across light calculations. This is something you CAN do in hand-coded shaders. So effects similar to \"Shadow to Opacity\" not possible to reproduce in the visual shader editor. The last light to touch the alpha output for a given pixel has no context about the other passes, it'll be overwriting it completely very time.\n\nThe fix is actually simple and I'm throwing a PR up for it next.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n* Just take a look at the input dropdown in the \"Light\" function of a visual shader graph, there's no way to access Alpha across light passes.\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n* Just take a look at the input dropdown in the \"Light\" function of a visual shader graph, there's no way to access Alpha across light passes.","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://ap